<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 378&#xA0;&#x2014; Metadata of Relief (&#xAB;ApplicationSchema&#xBB;)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_fcd3aa79-4e7b-b840-349a-2c0fafd3cc74" id="_fcd3aa79-4e7b-b840-349a-2c0fafd3cc74"></a><colgroup><col width="20%"/><col width="80%"/></colgroup><tbody><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="20.0%">Description:</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="80.0%"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3ca20585-3cf2-ab33-5eca-c778346b68c9" id="_3ca20585-3cf2-ab33-5eca-c778346b68c9"></a>The Relief module supports representation of the terrain. CityGML supports terrain representations at different levels of detail, reflecting different accuracies or resolutions. Terrain may be specified as a regular raster or grid, as a TIN, by break lines, and/or by mass points.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="20.0%">Parent package:</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="80.0%"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4a69662a-97fb-d541-831a-b9c5fa6b6b9d" id="_4a69662a-97fb-d541-831a-b9c5fa6b6b9d"></a>CityGML</p>
