        <div><a name="_d552ed1a-6e87-782e-3de8-2b91631596d2" id="_d552ed1a-6e87-782e-3de8-2b91631596d2"></a><h2>8.12.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Vegetation</h2>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 503&#xA0;&#x2014; Metadata of Vegetation (&#xAB;ApplicationSchema&#xBB;)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_fa55ea35-ead4-1364-7cbe-f1890f006086" id="_fa55ea35-ead4-1364-7cbe-f1890f006086"></a><colgroup><col width="20%"/><col width="80%"/></colgroup><tbody><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="20.0%">Description:</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="80.0%"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c28f8f5d-357a-4201-5517-cd774f6cf2f8" id="_c28f8f5d-357a-4201-5517-cd774f6cf2f8"></a>The Vegetation module supports representation of vegetation objects with vegetation-specific thematic classes. CityGML?s vegetation model distinguishes between solitary vegetation objects like trees, and vegetation areas which represent biotopes like forests or other plant communities.</p>
